1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:15,000
残酷な天使のように 少年よ 神話になれ

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:37,000
青い風が今 胸のドアを叩いても 私だけをただ見つめて 微笑んでるあなた

3
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:51,000
そっと触れるもの 求めることに夢中で 運命さえまだ知らない 痛い気な瞳

4
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:58,000
だけどいつか気づくでしょう その背中には

5
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,000
遥か未来 目指すための羽があること

6
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:14,000
残酷な天使の帝世 窓辺からやがて飛び立つ

7
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,000
ほとばしる熱いパッドスで 思い出を裏切るなら

8
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
この空を抱いて輝く 少年よ 神話になれ

9
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
ご視聴ありがとうございました

10
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
ご視聴ありがとうございました

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,000
心の centres

12
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
ゆいっぱい部活動

13
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,000
あ でも あなたの歴 새로沒有

14
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
あ genugか

15
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:57,000
ご視聴ありがとうございました

16
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:02,000
あ 永遠のおかしい

17
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,560
You damn f-

18
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:52,700
Thanks for letting us in, Shinji.

19
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:54,880
That rainstorm came out of nowhere.

20
00:02:55,180 --> 00:02:56,820
So, like, where's Misato?

21
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,140
She must still be asleep.

22
00:02:58,540 --> 00:03:00,340
She's been working all night a lot lately.

23
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:02,360
Yeah, she's got a tough job.

24
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:07,040
Well, then, I guess we've got to be quiet so that we don't wake Misato up, right?

25
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:08,000
Well...

26
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:08,360
Shh!

27
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:09,720
Hey!

28
00:03:10,660 --> 00:03:13,240
What the heck are these creeps doing in here?

29
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:13,660
Shhh!

30
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:14,420
Drying themselves?

31
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:17,080
Oh, sure. Talk about lame excuses!

32
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:20,720
Well, I'm changing in here, and if you peep, you're dead!

33
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:26,400
You stuck-up, becatistical little dude want to watch a snake changing its skin anyway!

34
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:28,820
She's sure full of herself.

35
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:30,520
Huh?

36
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:33,220
Mimi! Misato!

37
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:34,560
Did we wake you up?

38
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:36,600
Actually, I was already awake.

39
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,620
Thanks for asking, though.

40
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:42,440
Shinji, don't forget that we're having a harmonics test at the lab this evening.

41
00:03:42,540 --> 00:03:42,980
Oh, right.

42
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,900
Hey, Asuka, did you hear that?

43
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:46,100
Yes, ma'am!

44
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:46,920
Huh?

45
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,000
Wow!

46
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:52,120
I mean, congratulations on your promotion, Misato.

47
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:53,320
Yeah, congratulations.

48
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,160
You're too kind.

49
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:57,140
No, ma'am. You deserved it.

50
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,980
Well, I'll see you guys later.

51
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,180
Have fun!

52
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,040
See ya!

53
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:04,120
So, what's up?

54
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,860
Did something happen to Misato?

55
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,200
Haven't you seen her new badge?

56
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:10,080
It's got two stripes on it now.

57
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,420
Two stripes means that she's been promoted to major.

58
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:13,360
Promoted?

59
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:14,260
I did. I didn't notice.

60
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:16,060
Yeah, me neither.

61
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:17,700
Neither of you noticed?

62
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:19,660
What a bunch of lame-os.

63
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:23,760
Man, don't you guys ever pay attention to that poor, hard-working woman?

64
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:29,000
Do you have any idea of how hard it must be to take care of the two of you at her age?

65
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,280
I guess it's a good thing that some of us still have a little human compassion.

66
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:46,280
Units 0 and 2 are both on the edge of the contamination zone.

67
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:47,280
They've reached their limit.

68
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:50,400
Unit 1 can still tolerate a little more, though, can't he?

69
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:53,180
Lower the graph depth another 0.3.

70
00:04:53,180 --> 00:05:01,100
He's almost reached the contamination zone.

71
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:02,760
And he's still getting these readings?

72
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,280
He's just wonderful.

73
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:07,800
His harmonics and sync ratio are rapidly catching up with Asuka's.

74
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:09,980
He does have talent, doesn't he?

75
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:13,380
It's as if he was born to become a Nava pilot, isn't it?

76
00:05:14,020 --> 00:05:15,800
But that's not what Shinji wants.

77
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:18,040
I know he's not really happy here.

78
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:22,760
The test has been completed.

79
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:27,520
That was excellent work, Shinji.

80
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:28,540
What do you mean?

81
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:32,120
Your harmonics value has increased by 8 points since the last test.

82
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:33,200
That's very good.

83
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:35,740
But it's still 50 points below mine.

84
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:36,760
That's true.

85
00:05:36,940 --> 00:05:38,960
But 8 points in 10 days is amazing.

86
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:40,660
I don't think it's so great.

87
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:42,940
Okay, third child.

88
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:45,220
Enjoy your victory while you can.

89
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:49,600
I'll see you when you get home, jerk face.

90
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:54,180
And here's your message for Mr. Y in Tokyo, too.

91
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,820
And look, bud, having your first...

92
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:58,580
Oh, by the way, it's nice that you got promoted.

93
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:00,000
Thanks, Shinji.

94
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:03,120
But to tell you the truth, I'm not really all that thrilled with it.

95
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:04,340
Oh, I understand.

96
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:07,640
I'm not crazy about getting praised in public either.

97
00:06:08,020 --> 00:06:09,660
Especially when it's like earlier today.

98
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:12,000
All it did was make Asuka angry.

99
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,980
Why does she get so pissed off?

100
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:17,000
It's so stupid.

101
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,540
It bothers you, doesn't it?

102
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:21,520
It does.

103
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:24,900
Well, that's because you think too much about what others think.

104
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:29,320
Congratulations!

105
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:31,420
Way to go, Misato!

106
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:34,200
Thanks, you guys.

107
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:36,140
And thank you, Toji.

108
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,260
No, no.

109
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,040
This was Kensuke's idea.

110
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:43,780
That's right, I, Kensuke Ida, am the mastermind behind this dinner.

111
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:46,500
Oh, well, then thank you, Mr. Ida.

112
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,600
Oh, it was no problem.

113
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:50,700
It wasn't such a big deal, really.

114
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:54,080
Hey, by the way, just what is Hikari doing here?

115
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:56,000
I invited her, Doomkopf.

116
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:57,280
Yeah?

117
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,700
Did you invite Rei, too?

118
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:03,540
Well, I invited her, but she's not exactly the party type, you know?

119
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:06,020
Darn, why is Kaji so late?

120
00:07:06,020 --> 00:07:06,700
Kaji?

121
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:09,920
You mean that really cool-looking guy who never shaves?

122
00:07:10,420 --> 00:07:10,820
Yeah.

123
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:15,760
After hanging around these dorks all day, it's nice to know what a real man is like.

124
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:16,700
Real man?

125
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:20,120
So, kiddo, is it still difficult for you to be in this kind of situation?

126
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:21,400
I'm okay.

127
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:24,160
I'm just not used to being around so many people.

128
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:29,060
Why do they have to be so nosy?

129
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:35,700
Your promotion.

130
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:40,460
That means that someone must appreciate the kind of work you've been doing, right?

131
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:42,580
Yeah, I suppose so.

132
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,420
That's why they're all so happy for you.

133
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:47,820
But you don't look very happy at all.

134
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:49,640
Oh, I'm happy.

135
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:52,140
But that's not the reason I do what I do.

136
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,680
So, why did you join now?

137
00:07:58,520 --> 00:07:59,280
Oh, I don't know.

138
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:01,580
It's been a long time since I signed up, you know.

139
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:08,720
Oh, that's gotta be Kaji!

140
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:12,380
I came directly from headquarters.

141
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:14,280
We just happened to meet on the way.

142
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:15,940
A likely story.

143
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:17,420
You're not jealous, are you?

144
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:18,380
Hmm.

145
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,240
Absolutely not.

146
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:23,480
I'd like to give you my sincerest regards, Major Katsuragi.

147
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:26,540
I suppose I'll have to be polite to you from now on.

148
00:08:27,060 --> 00:08:27,260
Hmm.

149
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:28,720
And just what does that mean?

150
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:33,440
Well, you know that Commanders Ikari and Fiyutsuki have never left Japan at the same time before.

151
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:37,000
I guess they must really feel old Katsuragi here's dependable.

152
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:38,880
My father's left Japan again?

153
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:40,280
That's right, Shinji.

154
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:41,900
He's at the South Pole.

155
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:48,360
Once this was a living continent of Antarctica.

156
00:08:48,740 --> 00:08:50,120
Now it's an ocean of death.

157
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:51,580
The Pole.

158
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:53,460
Not just another name for hell.

159
00:08:54,020 --> 00:08:56,900
Nevertheless, mankind has returned to this wasteland.

160
00:08:56,900 --> 00:08:59,300
In the midst of death, we still live.

161
00:08:59,420 --> 00:09:01,760
That's because we're under the protection of science.

162
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:03,940
Science is what makes man powerful.

163
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:07,980
That kind of self-righteous arrogance is what caused the tragedy of 15 years ago.

164
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:09,220
The second impact.

165
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:12,540
And here, before us, is the end result.

166
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:15,300
This is a far greater punishment than mankind deserved.

167
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:17,240
This is the real Dead Sea.

168
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:21,500
Yet this is a world that has been purified and purged of the original sin.

169
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:25,280
I'd rather live in a world with people, no matter how stained this.

170
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:26,600
This is the bridge.

171
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:29,240
We've just received a telex from NERV headquarters.

172
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:32,280
An Angel has been detected in orbit above the Indian Ocean.

173
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:34,600
The Angel appeared about two minutes ago.

174
00:09:35,020 --> 00:09:37,180
Send recon satellite number six to that orbit.

175
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:39,080
T-minus two minutes to contact.

176
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,360
Target has been sighted.

177
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:43,660
Oh, it's enormous.

178
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:45,640
It's impressive, all right.

179
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:47,720
Recon six is now in range.

180
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:54,520
Commencing data search.

181
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:56,120
Commencing data transmission.

182
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:57,800
Data transmission complete.

183
00:09:57,800 --> 00:10:01,100
Was that an AT field?

184
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:01,840
Yes.

185
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,060
A new way of using one.

186
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,500
Look at the size of that tidal wave.

187
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:13,060
That's an AT field impact.

188
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:15,220
It uses kinetic energy, too.

189
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:17,560
This Angel is like a huge living bomb.

190
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:21,580
At least the first blast missed and hit the ocean.

191
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:26,080
However, the second shot hit closer to land, and for the last two hours, it's been steadily

192
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,480
correcting its error ratio.

193
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:29,360
So it's learning to aim itself.

194
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:32,160
We detonated an N2 aerial mine on it.

195
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,120
No effect.

196
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:35,000
The Angel has been hiding since then.

197
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:37,360
It's coming here, isn't it?

198
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:38,840
It's a safe bet.

199
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:40,120
And if it falls on us...

200
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,540
Then there'll be a third Ashinoka Lake, right?

201
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:47,520
Actually, this whole area will become an extension of the Pacific Ocean.

202
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:49,820
Can we contact Commander Ikari?

203
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:51,200
It's impossible.

204
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:52,940
We can't get through the Angel's jamming.

205
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:55,460
What about the Magi?

206
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:58,100
The Magi are unanimous in recommending evacuation.

207
00:10:59,120 --> 00:10:59,960
What will you do?

208
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:02,480
You're the one who's in charge of all this now.

209
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:07,580
Notify all the ministries concerned that I am issuing a special D-17 declaration.

210
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:11,840
All residents within a radius of 50 kilometers are to evacuate immediately.

211
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:14,640
Also, tell Matsushiro to back up the Magi.

212
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:16,340
Are we going to evacuate as well?

213
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:20,820
No, but it's not necessary to place everyone here at risk.

214
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:22,480
Your attention, please.

215
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:26,900
The government has announced a D-17 special declaration of emergency for this area.

216
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:30,280
All residents must evacuate to their designated locations.

217
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:35,640
Beginning with the Blocks 6 and 7, evacuate according to the directions of your district chief immediately.

218
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,460
The evacuation of the city is now complete.

219
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:44,820
The evacuation of all non-combatant and D-class personnel by Alarm C has been completed.

220
00:11:44,820 --> 00:11:50,340
You're not really serious, are you?

221
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:51,540
Yes, I am.

222
00:11:51,780 --> 00:11:55,060
You're willing to sacrifice all three Avas to satisfy your own ambitions?

223
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:58,540
The chance of success is 0.001%.

224
00:11:58,540 --> 00:12:00,280
Just one in 10,000.

225
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:02,280
Well, it's not 0.001%.

226
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:02,640
Well, it's not 0.001%.

227
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:04,420
I just trust the Avas.

228
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:08,300
Major Katsuragi, don't forget that I'm the one in charge now.

229
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:12,940
I have to do what I have to do.

230
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,200
Destroying the Angels is my duty.

231
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,160
Your duty?

232
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:17,260
You must be kidding.

233
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:19,520
This is to satisfy yourself, isn't it?

234
00:12:19,680 --> 00:12:21,620
This is just your revenge against the Angels.

235
00:12:21,620 --> 00:12:31,620
What?

236
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:34,580
You want us to catch it with our hands?

237
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:35,560
That's right.

238
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,300
We'll locate the Avas in an estimated drop zone.

239
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:42,020
Then, while maintaining your AT fields, you'll catch it before it hits the ground.

240
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,260
But what if it doesn't fall where you think it will?

241
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:46,760
Then there'll be a little boom.

242
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:49,320
But what if the Avas can't handle the impact?

243
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:50,660
We'll all be blown to the moon.

244
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:51,860
What are our chances?

245
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:53,240
I've got no idea.

246
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:54,980
Not so good, in my opinion.

247
00:12:55,860 --> 00:12:58,080
If we pull this off, it'll be a miracle.

248
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:00,420
Miracles aren't something that just happened.

249
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:02,140
They're something that people make happen.

250
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,540
We've got to be willing to sacrifice ourselves.

251
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:05,920
I'm sorry, Aska.

252
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,620
We've got no other choice.

253
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:09,060
This is the best plan.

254
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:11,420
How can you call something this crazy a plan?

255
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:13,200
I suppose I can't, really.

256
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:15,680
You can refuse to do it if you wish.

257
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:18,420
I see.

258
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:20,300
So you are okay with this?

259
00:13:20,660 --> 00:13:25,100
The regulations state here that you're all supposed to write out a will.

260
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:26,060
Have you done that yet?

261
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:27,320
I don't need to write one.

262
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:29,040
I'm not going to die just yet.

263
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:30,120
Neither do I.

264
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:31,780
There's no point to it.

265
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:33,840
Yeah, me neither.

266
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:35,360
Okay.

267
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:39,040
But when all of this is over, I'll treat all of you to a steak dinner, okay?

268
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:40,580
A steak dinner?

269
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:41,200
Yep.

270
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:42,080
Wow.

271
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:43,580
You won't forget, right?

272
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:45,360
I swear I won't.

273
00:13:50,740 --> 00:13:53,180
A steak dinner is supposed to impress us?

274
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:57,120
Does she really think we'd go crazy just for a dumb steak dinner?

275
00:13:57,480 --> 00:14:01,220
Man, the second impact generation has really got some cheap standards.

276
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:03,200
I suppose she just can't help it.

277
00:14:03,820 --> 00:14:08,220
Well, that wow you made sounded pretty enthusiastic to me, Shinji.

278
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:12,040
Well, it may not mean much to us, but it still means something to her, you know?

279
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:13,600
I suppose so.

280
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:15,740
Well, let's figure out where she's going to take us.

281
00:14:16,400 --> 00:14:18,980
Tokyo 3 Five Star Restaurant Directory.

282
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:21,660
You're going to be coming with us, right, First Child?

283
00:14:22,660 --> 00:14:23,920
I don't think so.

284
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:24,860
Why not?

285
00:14:26,020 --> 00:14:27,940
I dislike eating meat.

286
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:31,280
Angel's ECM jamming has caused us to lose track of it again.

287
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:34,200
Since it's impossible to calculate the exact location,

288
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:39,000
the Magi have estimated a probable drop zone radius from what little data we could collect.

289
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:40,140
This is it.

290
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:42,060
That's a huge area to cover!

291
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:44,720
It could drop on any of these locations?

292
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:47,460
Given the size of the target's AT field,

293
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:51,820
it could completely annihilate Nerve Headquarters simply by coming close with a near miss.

294
00:14:51,940 --> 00:14:55,160
So, we'll disperse the Avis so there's one at each of these three points.

295
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:57,040
What is this dispersal based on?

296
00:14:57,760 --> 00:14:58,520
A guess.

297
00:14:59,420 --> 00:15:00,060
A guess?

298
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,620
It's women's intuition.

299
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:03,440
Her woman's intuition.

300
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:06,780
Looks like our miracle's getting further and further away.

301
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:10,200
She plays the lottery a lot, and she never wins either.

302
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:10,940
Ooh.

303
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:13,680
Hey, Asuka.

304
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:14,480
What?

305
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:16,900
Why did you become an Ava pilot?

306
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:19,440
To show the world how great I am, of course.

307
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:22,400
So, it's a way of proving that you exist?

308
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:25,300
Yeah, I guess you could say that.

309
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:27,700
Why don't you ask Wonder Girl?

310
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:31,320
I've already talked with her about it.

311
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:32,300
Hmm.

312
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:34,680
So, you've been having secret meetings.

313
00:15:35,180 --> 00:15:36,500
No, it's not like that.

314
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:38,520
So, why do you do this?

315
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,300
I don't know.

316
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:42,260
Just what do you mean?

317
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:43,440
Are you stupid?

318
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:45,560
Uh, maybe I am.

319
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:46,620
Ah.

320
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:50,300
I suppose you really are.

321
00:15:50,300 --> 00:15:53,740
20 minutes to estimated time of impact.

322
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:57,100
The rest of you can leave now.

323
00:15:57,420 --> 00:15:58,980
I can take care of this situation.

324
00:15:59,480 --> 00:15:59,920
Sorry.

325
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:01,460
This is our job as well.

326
00:16:01,880 --> 00:16:04,920
Yeah, we can't let those kids risk their lives all by themselves.

327
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:06,180
Don't worry about the children.

328
00:16:06,180 --> 00:16:07,180
Don't worry about the children.

329
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:11,880
No matter how badly the Avas might get damaged, their AT fields will protect them.

330
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:15,520
Actually, the safest place to be right now is inside the Ava.

331
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:27,240
The other day, you wanted to know why I really joined Nerve.

332
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:30,700
It began with my father.

333
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:34,500
He lived for his work, to the exclusion of everything else.

334
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:37,300
I was never able to forgive him for that.

335
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:39,660
In fact, at times, I even hated him.

336
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:41,880
It sounds like my father.

337
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:45,120
He never really took care of me or my mother.

338
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:49,000
His friends always said that he was too sensitive and fragile.

339
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,640
But the truth was, he was just a weak person.

340
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:53,640
He didn't want to face reality.

341
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:57,280
So avoiding his family was easier than dealing with it.

342
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:01,200
When my mother decided to divorce him, I was actually happy.

343
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:04,520
I was so sick of hearing her cry herself to sleep.

344
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:10,440
And when my dad got upset about it, I actually laughed at him because I thought he got what he deserved.

345
00:17:12,100 --> 00:17:16,120
But then he sacrificed himself to save my life during this second impact.

346
00:17:16,120 --> 00:17:20,420
But then I didn't know whether I hated him or loved him.

347
00:17:21,060 --> 00:17:27,580
The only thing that was clear to me was that I wanted to destroy the angels who had caused the second impact.

348
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:30,440
And that's why I joined Nerve.

349
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:40,140
It might be that I still hate him and just want to avenge my father so that I can finally free myself from him.

350
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:42,400
It's the only way I can escape.

351
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:43,900
I mustn't run away.

352
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:44,980
I mustn't run away.

353
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:46,180
I mustn't run away.

354
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:47,600
I won't.

355
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:49,860
I won't run away.

356
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:51,360
The target has been sighted.

357
00:17:51,560 --> 00:17:52,660
Maximum magnification.

358
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:54,800
Distance, approximately 25,000.

359
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:56,280
The falling angel's been sighted.

360
00:17:57,140 --> 00:17:58,680
All Avas, get on your marks.

361
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:10,060
We can only give you a rough estimated trajectory based upon optical observations.

362
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:13,660
The magi will guide you until the estimated distance is 10,000 meters.

363
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:15,640
After that, you'll have to use your own judgment.

364
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:17,920
Remember, I'm placing my trust in you.

365
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:19,540
The angel is approaching.

366
00:18:19,780 --> 00:18:20,820
Distance, 20,000.

367
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:21,660
Right.

368
00:18:21,660 --> 00:18:22,820
Begin the operation.

369
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:24,160
Here we go.

370
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:28,700
Let's move out!

371
00:18:28,700 --> 00:18:45,500
Distance, 12,000.

372
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:57,920
Spreading A.T. field!

373
00:18:57,920 --> 00:19:18,840
Unit 2, expand your field!

374
00:19:18,980 --> 00:19:20,320
I'm already doing it!

375
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:25,620
Do it now!

376
00:19:25,620 --> 00:19:32,080
Ain't this!

377
00:19:32,080 --> 00:19:33,740
More!

378
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:50,640
Hmm.

379
00:19:50,640 --> 00:20:06,800
Our wireless communications have been restored.

380
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:10,080
We're receiving a transmission from Commander Ikari in Antarctica.

381
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:11,860
Connect him, please.

382
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:12,540
Yes, ma'am.

383
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:15,040
I apologize, sir.

384
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:18,940
Because of my irresponsible judgment, Unit 1 has incurred some damage.

385
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:21,620
I take full responsibility for this, sir.

386
00:20:21,860 --> 00:20:24,380
No. Destroying angels is an Ava's purpose.

387
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:27,240
It was fortunate that the amount of damage done was minimal.

388
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:29,720
Excellent work, Major Katsuragi.

389
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:32,500
Thank you, Commander.

390
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:35,240
And on that subject, is the pilot of Unit 1 there?

391
00:20:36,460 --> 00:20:36,940
Yes.

392
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:40,220
I've just read the report. Good work, Shinji.

393
00:20:42,820 --> 00:20:43,520
Yes, sir.

394
00:20:43,620 --> 00:20:47,300
Now, Major Katsuragi, I'll leave the handling of the rest of this in your hands.

395
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:48,080
Yes, sir.

396
00:20:48,940 --> 00:21:01,360
The next station is New Mianoshita. New Mianoshita. The door will open on the left side of the next station.

397
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:04,100
So, now you're going to have to fulfill your promise.

398
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:05,620
Well, of course I will.

399
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:09,140
I went and pulled some large bills for my account so that I could cover everything.

400
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,580
Of course, now I'm broke.

401
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,740
A ramen place?

402
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:16,300
Well, we know how poor you are, Misato.

403
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:17,700
This will be fine.

404
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:20,920
And since there's no meat, Wonder Girl will be joining us.

405
00:21:21,020 --> 00:21:22,960
One garlic ramen with no roast pork.

406
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:25,520
I'll have shark spin ramen with roast pork.

407
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:26,480
Super size it!

408
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:27,100
There you go.

409
00:21:29,620 --> 00:21:30,880
Say, Misato.

410
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:32,000
Yeah?

411
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:38,680
I think I finally understood the good part about being praised by someone when I heard my father's words today.

412
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:45,860
And I also realized that the reason I pilot my Ava is to hear those words from him.

413
00:21:49,140 --> 00:21:51,060
Now, wait a second.

414
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:52,980
That's why you're a pilot?

415
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:55,940
Jeez, you really are an idiot.

416
00:21:55,940 --> 00:22:22,040
You really are an idiot?

417
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:32,220
In another world, darling kiss me

418
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:36,320
Fill my heart with some

419
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:40,860
And let me sing forever more

420
00:22:40,860 --> 00:22:44,460
You are all I know

421
00:22:44,460 --> 00:22:49,000
For all I worship and I do

422
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:55,580
In another world, please be true

423
00:22:55,580 --> 00:23:04,180
In another world, I love you

424
00:23:04,180 --> 00:23:08,860
The Magi, the trio of supercomputers

425
00:23:08,860 --> 00:23:11,240
that command all of Nerve headquarters are under attack

426
00:23:11,240 --> 00:23:13,840
As problems mount and central dogma is invaded

427
00:23:13,840 --> 00:23:16,760
Nerve is forced to accept a course of self-destruction

428
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:18,780
It all happens in the next episode

429
00:23:18,780 --> 00:23:19,840
Angel Invasion

